// Byline: Claude Code · Opus 5.5 · 2026-09-26.
//
// Tailscale Service svc:authentik (VIP + https://authentik.tilapia-skilift.ts.net), hosted by
// the tagged service host that runs the Authentik app (today ovh-app, 100.72.169.40).
// Service definition (register once through the API): ports tcp:443 and tcp:9075, tag:docker.
// Apply on the service host, then approve that host for the service:
//   tailscale serve set-config --service=svc:authentik authentik-serve.hujson
//   tailscale serve advertise svc:authentik
//
// tcp:443  HTTPS endpoint, the owner's tailnet door to the Authentik admin UI. No login
//          barrier is added for tailnet clients beyond Authentik's own admin sign-in.
// tcp:9075 raw TCP forwarder, Traefik's internal hop for auth.int.mitechconsult.com and every
//          public forward-auth check. It is raw TCP on purpose: Serve's HTTP proxy rewrites
//          X-Forwarded-Host and X-Forwarded-For, which breaks forward-auth.
//
// Both targets are the host's own tailnet address, so Authentik always sees the socket peer
// 100.72.169.40 (TRAEFIK_PROXY_CIDR=100.72.169.40/32 in the Authentik Coolify app). Authentik
// publishes that port only on the tailnet address (deploy/authentik.yaml). Never funnel this.
{
  "version": "0.0.1",
  "services": {
    "svc:authentik": {
      "endpoints": {
        "tcp:443": "http://100.72.169.40:9075",
        "tcp:9075": "tcp://100.72.169.40:9075"
      }
    }
  }
}
